o mastery or learning-effect claims are inferred.","identity":"Practice exports and immutable scientific reference exports remain separate. Target-bound RAM teaching copies retain a full original expert request with a teaching notice and manual Run, never pretending to be an existing notebook/project record.","integration":"The original scattering-phase disclosure is lazy. Existing mode, source-import and ZnO material routes point to that lesson. Obsolete whole-site no-Phonopy claims are corrected while the one-dimensional model and all old exercises remain intact."},"verification":["Independent nonorthogonal-coordinate, phase-convention, complex-arithmetic, mass, thermal-tensor, cutoff and finite-candidate tests accompany actual derivation and source-bound grade replies.","Mixed boolean/numeric answers, forged references, stale source fingerprints, malformed complex matrices and unsupported science conventions are explicitly exercised.","The actual UI and application host verify partial drafts, both-point copies, assisted reference access, manual Run, raw export identity, request ownership and detached/late callbacks.","Legacy numerical references are genuinely recomputed before source identities change; English, formulas, source extraction and published bytes are separate release gates."],"boundaries":["The classroom default is a fixed sourced harmonic ZnO mode, not a measured spectrum, generated force constants, full thermal mesh or convergence certification.","Changing G changes Cartesian projection and structural phase together. A finite pair refutes only the named candidates under the declared source and conventions.","The numerical grader checks fixed-gauge components with explicit tolerances; it does not certify arbitrary proofs, material identity, unique reasoning or course mastery.","The general expert tool retains its separate creation/annihilation, full-Q, supplied-thermal-tensor and custom-source contract."],"rawInputIdentities":[{"path":"dist/data/exam